    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="0703" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/3761½a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 3, 1917</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I send you a tentative
                    draft of a proclamation of which I spoke to you yesterday afternoon and which,
                    it seems to me, should be issued immediately upon the passage of the Joint
                    Resolution which I assume Congress will adopt.</p>
                <p>Will you please advise me whether this meets with your wishes in order that we
                    may prepare the proclamation so that it will issue without delay?</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d598-a1.xml" xpointer="d598-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
